  "question": {
    "text": "A coin is placed on a disc. The coefficient of friction between the coin and the disc is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi></math>. If the distance of the coin from the center of the disc is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, the maximum angular velocity which can be given to the disc, so that the coin does not slip away, is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><msqrt><mi>r</mi><mi>g</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0033_c388805ede2a.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 202px;\"/></p><p>Normal force acting on the coin is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>.</p><p>Required friction force to provide centripetal force for the coin is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi></math> and maximum value of static friction force available is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math>.</p><p>For limiting condition, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
}